  "goodToKnow": "Der Rummel is a funfair, especially in northern and eastern Germany (auf den Rummel gehen); elsewhere it's die Kirmes, das Volksfest or, in Bavaria, die Dult. It also means hype or fuss: der Medienrummel, viel Rummel um nichts. Den Rummel kennen means to know the score. Hamburg's Dom is one of Germany's biggest fairs, held three times a year. It has no plural."
